    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "ASK",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — the command typed",
      "narration_text": "In the terminal: ask Claude to write a Python CLI called predlock with two subcommands. Lock takes a text string, appends the UTC timestamp, the text, and its SHA-256 hash as a JSON line to predlock.log, and prints the hash. Resolve takes a hash prefix and an outcome text, finds the locked prediction by hash, appends the outcome, and prints prediction and outcome side by side plus 'HASH VERIFIED' if the stored text still hashes to the given hash.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "claude \"Write a Python CLI 'predlock' with two subcommands:\n(1) 'lock <text>' → append\n    {utc_timestamp, text, sha256(text)}\n    as JSON line to predlock.log, print the hash\n(2) 'resolve <hash> <outcome_text>' → find locked\n    prediction by hash, append outcome, print\n    prediction vs outcome + HASH VERIFIED or MISMATCH\"",
            "topic": "COMPUTATIONAL SKEPTICISM — HONESTY",
            "segment": "PREDICTION-LOCK HARNESS",
            "greeting": "",
            "runningText": "generating prediction-lock CLI…",
            "output": [],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T17:48:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "CODE",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — read the output before running",
      "narration_text": "Read the two functions before running. Lock does three things: compute SHA-256 of the text, build a JSON record with the timestamp, and append it to the log — one line, append-only, never overwritten. Resolve does one verification: it reads the stored text back from the log and hashes it again. If the hash still matches, the prediction was not edited. If it doesn't, it was. The tamper-evidence is not cryptographic; it's structural. The log is the audit trail.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "predlock.py",
            "code": "# predlock.py — Claude Code output\nimport hashlib, json, datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nLOG = Path(\"predlock.log\")\n\ndef lock(text: str) -> str:\n    h = hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()\n    record = {\n        \"utc\": datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat(),\n        \"text\": text,\n        \"sha256\": h,\n    }\n    with LOG.open(\"a\") as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(record) + \"\\n\")\n    return h  # print this; you can't re-derive it later\n\ndef resolve(hash_prefix: str, outcome: str):\n    for line in LOG.read_text().splitlines():\n        r = json.loads(line)\n        if r[\"sha256\"].startswith(hash_prefix):\n            verified = (\n                hashlib.sha256(r[\"text\"].encode()).hexdigest()\n                == r[\"sha256\"]\n            )\n            print(f\"PREDICTION: {r['text']}\")\n            print(f\"OUTCOME:    {outcome}\")\n            print(\"HASH VERIFIED\" if verified else \"HASH MISMATCH\")",
            "sparkLine": "PREDICTION-LOCK HARNESS"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T17:48:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "OUTPUT — run",
      "role_note": "screen-recording — lock before probe, resolve after, then tamper test",
      "narration_text": "Lock a prediction before running the probe: 'I expect ECE on the shifted slice to be under point-one.' Hash prints. Run the probe — ECE comes back at point-nineteen. Resolve with the hash: prediction prints, outcome prints, HASH VERIFIED. The gap is visible and real. Now edit the locked line in the log — change 'under point-one' to 'around point-two' — and resolve again. HASH MISMATCH. The edit is detectable.",
      "visual_intent": "screen-recording: predlock lock (hash prints) → probe runs (ECE=0.19) → predlock resolve (HASH VERIFIED, gap visible) → log edited manually → predlock resolve again (HASH MISMATCH)",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "terminal: predlock demo",
            "code": "$ python predlock.py lock \"ECE on shifted slice < 0.10\"\nHash: a3f7c2d1\n\n[...probe runs, ECE = 0.19...]\n\n$ python predlock.py resolve a3f7c2d1 \"ECE = 0.19\"\nPREDICTION: ECE on shifted slice < 0.10\nOUTCOME:    ECE = 0.19\nHASH VERIFIED\n\n[...manually edit log line...]\n\n$ python predlock.py resolve a3f7c2d1 \"ECE = 0.19\"\nHASH MISMATCH  ← edit detected",
            "sparkLine": "PREDICTION-LOCK HARNESS"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
